.Dd January 25, 2026
.Dt DEVICE_UNREGISTER 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm device_unregister
.Nd remove a device from the system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/device.h
.Ft int
.Fn device_unregister "struct device *dev"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn device_unregister
function removes a device from the system topology.
.Pp
It performs the following actions:
.Bl -enum
.It
Removes the device from its attached bus (acquiring the bus lock).
.It
Removes the device from its parent's children list.
.It
Orphans all child devices by setting their parent pointer to NULL.
.El
.Pp
After calling this function, the device structure is still allocated but is effectively detached from the hierarchy.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn device_unregister
function returns 0 on success, or -1 if
.Fa dev
is NULL.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr device 9 ,
.Xr device_register 9 ,
.Xr device_create 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn device_unregister
kernel interface first appeared in Substrate.
